{
  "body0": "The boundary condition nobody can renegotiate: False sensor returns does not negotiate and does not stop. The false sensor returns versus Custos Echo-58 Belt IV Charter is the headline; the secular decline in conditions at Custos Echo-58 Belt IV is the data. The residual no published account explains: corporate records were altered. Every model of the dispute shares one input: both sides armed their inspectors in the same quarter. The system has entered sustained-conflict operations by every measurable proxy. The principals are Gamma Ledger Trust and Tau Reticuli Cohort; the measurable damage accumulates at the derelict fleet cluster. Recruiters from both sides work the same ration queue, one table apart. Instruments at Gamma Ledger Trust record the dispute between the derelict fleet cluster and Tau Reticuli Cohort as a rising baseline of scarcity: the freight surcharge that lands on them no matter who wins. Reduced to observables, the driver is this — the safety margins were drawn before Derelict fleet cluster started moving. Longshore crews demand danger pay in scrip that clears the same day. Seismic and thermal baselines for Custos Echo-58 Belt IV are extrapolated from Custos Echo-58 Belt IV Charter's single-point coverage. Above ground, Gamma Ledger Trust holds the sole operating license for Custos Echo-58 Belt VI; the renewal process has no public docket.",
  "spineEdgeType": "DESTABILIZES",
  "spineSummary": "The perturbation from the false sensor returns now exceeds Custos Echo-58 Belt IV Charter's tolerance margin.",
}
`;

