{
  "body0": "Granite Reach Water Concession wants the authority to declare what counts as contaminated; Iron Compact Freight Guild guards the margin that keeps the lights on; Kestrel-Locke Salvage Concern gets rationed air while the principals negotiate. Underneath it runs a complication nobody prices openly: Granite Reach Water Concession turned on Iron Compact Freight Guild after the first audit. The arbitration hall stands empty; its clerks now work security rotations. Strip away the filings and the cause is plain — the safety margins were drawn before Derelict fleet cluster started moving. The derelict fleet cluster presses, Danfeng's Flare Belt III holds, and Danfeng's Flare Belt III Cylinder pays for both: family on both sides of the picket line. Evacuation lighters hold at ready-station through every work shift. The principals are the first-wave ghost colony and Danfeng's Flare Belt III; the casualty ledger, so far, is kept at Danfeng's Flare Belt III Cylinder. And there is the part no one says at the negotiating table: the quarantine is political. Prices quoted to the first-wave ghost colony and Danfeng's Flare Belt III differ by a margin every vendor denies. Danfeng's Flare Belt III carries Danfeng's Flare Belt III Cylinder on its surface.",
