exports[`spine tone × edge type voice matrix > tone=cinematic: spine prose reads in tone voice 1`] = `
{
  "body0": "The fuse is lit at both ends and burning politely. The trojan megaswarm wants the right to set tariffs no one else can audit. Calvera-10 IV wants tomorrow. Calvera-10 IV - Moon I Hold wants the freight surcharge to stop climbing. Longshore crews demand danger pay in scrip that clears the same day. It has not gone loud yet; the quiet is the expensive kind. Carrion Synod sharpens, Crown of Dust Pact braces, and Calvera-10 V learns to sleep in a pressure suit. Both camps bid on the same salvage lots just to keep them from each other. The shortage memorial is a single empty tank, left ungauged on purpose. When the phase-stable superconductive lattice and Calvera-10 IV - Moon I Hold finally close, it will be Calvera-10 V Platform standing between them, holding a clinic that treats casualties from either camp and bills neither. What is left is wreckage with paperwork attached. And Carrion Synod doesn't post guards at Calvera-10 V anymore. It doesn't need to. Every generation at Calvera-10 IV - Moon I Hold swears it will leave Calvera-10 IV; every generation digs one level deeper. There, Cut the line that carries Phase-stable superconductive lattice and Calvera-10 V Platform becomes a memorial with a docking ring.",
